This paper describes the development of a \LaTeX{} package
	to create a bookshelf image from a \BibTeX{} file, suitable for
	use as a background for a video call in Zoom, Skype, or
	similar. Each entry is typeset as the spine of a book with
	title and author, using a randomly-selected font, color, and
	size. The paper describes the problems of random choice with
	both fixed-length and [potentially] endless lists, and the
	algorithm used to fit the author and title onto the spine. The
	package is available as \textsf{bookshelf} on
	\acro{CTAN} for inspection and testing.\par 
